<body>
  <section class="slide"><div class="slide-content">
    <span class="badge">ByteDance Seed · Qwen2.5-32B base model · No SFT data</span>
    <h1>VAPO: Value-Model-Based RL for Advanced Reasoning</h1>
    <p class="sub">AIME 2024 score: <strong>60.4</strong> (reported as 60 on comparison charts), surpassing DAPO by 10+ points.</p>
    <div class="row" style="margin-top:clamp(0.8rem,2vh,1.4rem)">
      <div class="card col"><div class="small">Headline result</div><div class="kpi">60.4</div><div class="small">AIME 2024</div></div>
      <div class="card col"><div class="small">Previous strong baseline</div><div class="kpi" style="color:#ffcf73">50</div><div class="small">DAPO</div></div>
      <div class="card col"><div class="small">Gap</div><div class="kpi" style="color:#7df57a">+10.4</div><div class="small">absolute points</div></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>Why Value Models? Finer Credit Assignment for Long CoT</h2>
    <div class="flow" style="margin-top:clamp(0.5rem,1.4vh,1rem)">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Value-model-free RL (GRPO / DAPO)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Trajectory-level advantage applied uniformly.</li>
          <li>Weak token-level signal for multi-step reasoning.</li>
          <li>Harder to identify which steps caused success/failure.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arrow">→</div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Value-model-based RL (VAPO)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Per-token value estimates enable granular credit assignment.</li>
          <li>Improves optimization for long, structured chains-of-thought.</li>
          <li>Outperforms value-free methods when stability issues are solved.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="footer">Motivation from source brief: long-CoT reasoning requires fine-grained credit, not uniform trajectory rewards.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>Three Challenges in Value-Model-Based RL for Long-CoT</h2>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col card challenge"><h3>1) Value bias</h3><p>Long trajectories and bootstrapping errors bias value targets, destabilizing policy/value co-training.</p></div>
      <div class="col card challenge"><h3>2) Heterogeneous lengths</h3><p>Short and long responses require different bias-variance tradeoffs for advantage estimation.</p></div>
      <div class="col card challenge"><h3>3) Reward sparsity</h3><p>Sparse outcomes in long CoT reduce learning signal density and slow optimization.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>VAPO Framework: Challenge → Technique Mapping</h2>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col card">
        <h3>Challenge Axis</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Bias from long trajectories</li>
          <li>Length-dependent bias/variance</li>
          <li>Sparse rewards in long reasoning</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="col card solution">
        <h3>Integrated VAPO Components</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Value-Pretraining</strong> + <strong>Decoupled-GAE</strong> → stabilize value estimation</li>
          <li><strong>Length-adaptive GAE</strong> → dynamic λ by response length</li>
          <li><strong>Clip-Higher</strong>, <strong>Token-level Loss</strong>, <strong>Positive Example LM Loss</strong>, <strong>Group-Sampling</strong> → densify/useful gradients under sparse rewards</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="footer">Framework objective: make value-model-based RL practical and superior for advanced reasoning.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>Length-Adaptive GAE: Dynamic λ for Variable-Length Responses</h2>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col card">
        <h3>Core mechanism</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>λ is adjusted as a function of response length.</li>
          <li>Short responses use lower λ → lower variance.</li>
          <li>Long responses use higher λ → lower bias.</li>
          <li>Targets heterogeneous sequence regimes in one trainer.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="col card">
        <h3>Conceptual bias-variance control</h3>
        <div class="bar-wrap"><div>Short CoT</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:35%"></div></div><div>low λ</div></div>
        <div class="bar-wrap"><div>Medium CoT</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:58%"></div></div><div>mid λ</div></div>
        <div class="bar-wrap"><div>Long CoT</div><div class="track"><div class="fill vapo" style="width:82%"></div></div><div>high λ</div></div>
        <p class="small">Ablation evidence: removing Length-adaptive GAE reduces AIME from 60 to 45 (−15).</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>Main Results: VAPO Leads AIME 2024</h2>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col card">
        <div class="bar-wrap"><div>Vanilla PPO</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:8%"></div></div><div>5</div></div>
        <div class="bar-wrap"><div>DeepSeek-R1-Zero-Qwen-32B</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:78%"></div></div><div>47</div></div>
        <div class="bar-wrap"><div>DAPO</div><div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width:83%"></div></div><div>50</div></div>
        <div class="bar-wrap"><div><strong>VAPO</strong></div><div class="track"><div class="fill vapo" style="width:100%"></div></div><div><strong>60</strong></div></div>
        <p class="small">Headline in brief: 60.4 reported; comparison chart uses integer 60.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col card">
        <h3>Training trajectory (Figure 2)</h3>
        <img class="figure" src="/app/benchmark/assets/figure_2.jpg" alt="Figure 2 training curve" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>Training Efficiency: SOTA in ~5K Steps</h2>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col card">
        <img class="figure" src="/app/benchmark/assets/figure_2.jpg" alt="AIME over training steps" />
        <p class="small">VAPO reaches ~60 around step 5,000; DAPO ~50 around step 5,500.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="col card">
        <img class="figure" src="/app/benchmark/assets/figure_3.jpg" alt="Mean response length over training" />
        <p class="small">VAPO reaches ~6,000-token responses vs DAPO ~4,500, indicating longer reasoning chains.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>Ablation: Component Contributions to AIME 2024</h2>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col card">
        <table class="table">
          <thead><tr><th>Configuration</th><th>AIME 2024</th><th>Δ vs Full</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Full VAPO</td><td><strong>60</strong></td><td>—</td></tr>
            <tr><td>w/o Value-Pretraining</td><td>11</td><td>-49</td></tr>
            <tr><td>w/o Decoupled-GAE</td><td>33</td><td>-27</td></tr>
            <tr><td>w/o Length-adaptive GAE</td><td>45</td><td>-15</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="col card">
        <h3>Interpretation</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Value-Pretraining is dominant</strong>: removing it collapses performance from 60 to 11.</li>
          <li>Decoupled-GAE and Length-adaptive GAE are both necessary for top-end performance.</li>
          <li>Ablation supports VAPO as an integrated system, not a single trick.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="slide"><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>Key Takeaways and Implications</h2>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col card">
        <ul>
          <li>Value-model-based RL can outperform value-free methods for complex reasoning when engineered for long-CoT regimes.</li>
          <li>Length-adaptive GAE is critical for heterogeneous response lengths.</li>
          <li>Value-Pretraining is the highest-impact component (−49 points when removed).</li>
          <li>VAPO reaches SOTA quickly (~5K steps) with stable training and no reported crashes across runs.</li>
          <li>Future reasoning model development should co-design objective, estimator, and stabilization stack.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="col card">
        <h3>Bottom line</h3>
        <p class="sub">“Value-model-based RL is back — with the right engineering.”</p>
        <p class="small">All claims and numbers sourced from <code>source_brief.md</code>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>
</body>
</html>
