  <section class="slide"><div class="slide-content">
    <h2>Why Value Models? Finer Credit Assignment for Long CoT</h2>
    <div class="flow" style="margin-top:clamp(0.5rem,1.4vh,1rem)">
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Value-model-free RL (GRPO / DAPO)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Trajectory-level advantage applied uniformly.</li>
          <li>Weak token-level signal for multi-step reasoning.</li>
          <li>Harder to identify which steps caused success/failure.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="arrow">→</div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>Value-model-based RL (VAPO)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Per-token value estimates enable granular credit assignment.</li>
          <li>Improves optimization for long, structured chains-of-thought.</li>
          <li>Outperforms value-free methods when stability issues are solved.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="footer">Motivation from source brief: long-CoT reasoning requires fine-grained credit, not uniform trajectory rewards.</p>
